{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The checkpoint is useful, but its current guarantee is weaker than the comment claims. It only promotes the top three fast-checked candidates; if those fail older toolchains, a lower-ranked fully surviving candidate is never tested. If the final file is invalid and none of those three survives, it writes the invalid final candidate back instead of the known-good original. Concurrent same-problem episodes can also share trials because scoping is timestamp-only.\n\nFor trace quality, raw rollouts are worth retaining. The distilled trace currently drops the wrapper ID and labels the whole trajectory only with the post-checkpoint score, which can credit the agent’s final actions with a candidate restored by the runner. I’ll make these distinctions explicit in the recommendation rather than expanding this audit into a logging rewrite."}}
